Z||000006||Loki||09-25-2001||02:32 PM||||Hey MinnGreen...  I have the 2057's in stock now.  The ones that act as both parking and stop lights. waiting on the others to come in. Will get a few and let you know how much. I called APC on this and from what they said the 2057 is the bulb you wouldneed for the parking/stop bulbs. Soon as i get em ill let ya know.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||09-25-2001||04:04 PM||||Loki... did you find out if you could get the same bulb in Amber for the signal lights?  And do you have a reference manual at work that lists the correct bulb numbers for the backup lights and backlites for the "Pontiac"?||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||09-25-2001||04:28 PM||||In the fastback tails lights, all bulbs are standard bulbs. The signal/brake bulbs are 1157's. The tail and reverse bulbs are 1156's<BR>and the PONTIAC bulbs are 194's.<P> For amber tinted bulbs you get the ones with  the  a    after the number, 1157a for example.<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rick 88||09-25-2001||04:36 PM||||Minn,<P>If you want your "Pontiac" to be brighter than original you can substitute 906 bulbs for the originals with no problems. They will not damage the sockets and are considerably brighter. <P>Hope this helps,<P>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000010||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||10:33 AM||||Jelly are you sure about that?  My tail and brake lights are both red, signal lights are amber, and reverse lights white.  How could the tail/signal lights have two different brightnesses with a single filament bulb, and why would the signal lights use a two filament bulb when only a single source is driving the lights.<BR>In my car the tail/stop bulbs are ll57s and the signal & reverse lights both use 1156.  Your mileage may vary...||||reg||1
Z||000011||speed1||09-26-2001||07:35 PM||||For the fastbacks the owners manual and applications books list the brake/tail as 2057, directional 1156, backup 1156, pontiac logo 194.  I am not sure but the 2057 and 1157 look exactly the same.  I think that the 1157 has a brighter tailight element, but don't quote me on that.||||reg||1
